#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1
msgid "Package Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:3
msgid ""
"moon uses a package file to identify and describe a package. The legacy "
"format is `moon.pkg.json`, and the new format is `moon.pkg`. For full "
"JSON schema, please check [moon's "
"repository](https://github.com/moonbitlang/moon/blob/main/crates/moonbuild/template/pkg.schema.json)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:7
msgid ""
"Support for `moon.pkg.json` is deprecated. New projects should use "
"`moon.pkg`; existing JSON configuration can be migrated with `moon fmt` "
"as described below."
msgstr ""
"`moon.pkg.json` のサポートは非推奨です。新しいプロジェクトでは `moon.pkg` を使ってください。既存の JSON "
"設定は、以下の説明に従って `moon fmt` で移行できます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:11
msgid "New format (`moon.pkg`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:13
msgid ""
"The new format is a concise DSL. You can generate or reformat it from an "
"existing `moon.pkg.json` with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:16
msgid "moon -C <module_dir> fmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:20 ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:318
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:22
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/virtual\",\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")\n"
"\n"
"options(\n"
"  overrides: [ \"moonbit-community/language/packages/implement\" ],\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:26
msgid ""
"In `moon.pkg`, dependencies are declared in an `import { ... }` block. "
"Use `@alias` to set a custom alias:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:29 ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:196
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgA\",\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgC\" @c,\n"
"  \"moonbitlang/core/builtin\",\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:33
msgid ""
"Most fields from `moon.pkg.json` can be represented in an `options(...)` "
"block. Stable declarations such as `formatter` and `pkgtype` have "
"dedicated top-level forms. Legacy keys that contain `-` must be quoted "
"when they are used inside `options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:38
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"virtual\": { \"has-default\": true },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:42
msgid "The `moon.pkg` format allows comments `//...`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:44
msgid "Full syntax of `moon.pkg` is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:46
msgid ""
"moon_pkg ::= statement*\n"
"statement ::= import | assign | apply\n"
"\n"
"import ::= \"import\" \"{\" (import_item \",\")* import_item? \"}\" "
"import_kind?\n"
"import_item ::= STRING (\"@\" PKG_NAME)?\n"
"import_kind ::= \"for\" STRING\n"
"\n"
"assign ::= LIDENT \"=\" expr\n"
"\n"
"apply ::= LIDENT \"(\" (argument \",\")* argument? \")\"\n"
"argument ::= LIDENT \":\" expr | STRING \":\" expr  \n"
"\n"
"expr ::= array | object | apply | STRING | INT | \"true\" | \"false\"\n"
"array ::= \"[\" (expr \",\")* expr? \"]\"\n"
"object ::= \"{\" (field \",\")* field? \"}\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:64
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:66
msgid ""
"The package name is not configurable; it is determined by the directory "
"name of the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:68
msgid "Formatter"
msgstr "フォーマッタ"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:70
msgid ""
"The `formatter` field configures `moon fmt` for this package. Currently "
"it supports `ignore`, a list of file names that the formatter should "
"skip."
msgstr ""
"`formatter` フィールドは、このパッケージに対する `moon fmt` "
"の設定を行います。現在は、フォーマッタがスキップするファイル名の一覧である `ignore` をサポートしています。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:73
msgid ""
"This is useful for generated files or files that you intentionally keep "
"in a different format. Files produced by `pre-build` are already skipped "
"automatically, so `formatter.ignore` is mainly for additional files you "
"want to exclude."
msgstr ""
"これは、生成ファイルや、意図的に別の形式のままにしておきたいファイルに便利です。`pre-build` "
"で生成されたファイルはすでに自動でスキップされるため、`formatter.ignore` は主に追加で除外したいファイルのために使います。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md
msgid "moon.pkg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:82
msgid "formatter(ignore: [\"generated.mbt\", \"snapshot.mbt\"])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md
msgid "moon.pkg.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:89
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"formatter\": {\n"
"    \"ignore\": [\"generated.mbt\", \"snapshot.mbt\"]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:100
msgid "Package type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:102
msgid ""
"Use one `pkgtype` declaration to specify what a package builds. For "
"example, an executable package uses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:105
msgid "pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:109
msgid ""
"The available kinds are `library`, `executable`, and `foreign_library`. "
"`library` is the default. `executable` replaces the legacy `options(\"is-"
"main\": true)`, while `foreign_library` replaces the legacy "
"`options(link: true)`. These kinds are alternatives and must not be "
"declared together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:115
msgid ""
"In a foreign-library package, `#export_name` assigns a stable symbol name"
" to a public, non-generic function in generated Wasm, JavaScript, or C "
"output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:118
msgid ""
"#export_name(\"attr_add\")\n"
"pub fn add_by_attr(n : Int) -> Int {\n"
"  n + 42\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:125
msgid ""
"MoonBit currently requires export names to be valid C symbol identifiers "
"and unique within the package, regardless of the selected backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:129
msgid ""
"Known compiler issue: `#export_name` currently applies its C-symbol-"
"identifier restriction to every backend. WebAssembly export names are "
"UTF-8 strings and are not limited to C identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:134
msgid ""
"The attribute cannot be used on generic functions or functions with "
"optional arguments. Prefer `#export_name` over backend-specific `exports`"
" link configuration for new exports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:138
msgid ""
"Export declarations are scoped to the package that produces the artifact."
" An attribute or `exports` configuration in a dependency applies when "
"that dependency is built as its own artifact, but it does not add symbols"
" to a downstream package's artifact. Define and export a wrapper in the "
"exporting package to expose dependency functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:145
msgid ""
"The native backend does not currently support exporting a "
"`foreign_library` package as a linkable library artifact, including "
"shared libraries such as a `.dll` or `.so`."
msgstr ""
"native バックエンドは現在、`foreign_library` パッケージをリンク可能なライブラリアーティファクトとしてエクスポートできません。"
"これには `.dll` や `.so` などの共有ライブラリも含まれます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:151
msgid "is-main (deprecated)"
msgstr "is-main（非推奨）"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:153
msgid ""
"The `is-main` field is deprecated. It is still accepted for compatibility"
" with existing package files, but new and migrated `moon.pkg` files "
"should use `pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")` instead. The following legacy "
"declarations are equivalent to that `pkgtype` declaration:"
msgstr ""
"`is-main` フィールドは非推奨です。既存のパッケージファイルとの互換性のため引き続き使用できますが、新規または移行後の "
"`moon.pkg` では `pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")` を使用してください。次の旧形式の宣言は、この "
"`pkgtype` 宣言と同等です。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:158
msgid ""
"The output of the linking process depends on the backend. When this field"
" is set to `true`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:160
msgid ""
"For the Wasm and `wasm-gc` backends, a standalone WebAssembly module will"
" be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:161
msgid "For the `js` backend, a standalone JavaScript file will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:167
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"is-main\": true,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:176
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"is-main\": true\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:184
msgid "Importing dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:186
msgid "Import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:188
msgid ""
"The `import` field is used to specify other packages that a package "
"depends on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:190
msgid ""
"For example, the following imports `pkgA` and `pkgC`, aliasing `pkgC` to "
"`c`. User can write `@c` to access definitions from `pkgC`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:202
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"import\": [\n"
"        \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgA\",\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"path\": \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgC\",\n"
"            \"alias\": \"c\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"moonbitlang/core/builtin\"\n"
"    ]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:209
msgid ""
"Most core packages are not special here: if you use `@json`, `@test`, or "
"other ordinary core aliases, add the corresponding `moonbitlang/core/...`"
" package to `import` to avoid `core_package_not_imported` warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:213
msgid ""
"`prelude` is the exception. It is available by default, so the names it "
"exposes do not need an explicit package import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:216
msgid "Test import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:218
msgid ""
"The test import is used to specify other packages that the black-box test"
" package of this package depends on, with the same format as `import`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:223
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"  \"path/to/package2\" @pkg2,\n"
"} for \"test\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:231
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"test-import\": {\n"
"    \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"path\": \"path/to/package2\",\n"
"      \"alias\": \"pkg2\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:245
msgid ""
"The `test-import-all` field is used to specify whether all public "
"definitions from the package being tested should be imported (`true`) by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:247
msgid "White-box test import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:249
msgid ""
"The white-box test import is used to specify other packages that the "
"white-box test package of this package depends on, with the same format "
"as `import`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:254
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"  \"path/to/package2\" @pkg2,\n"
"} for \"wbtest\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:262
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"wbtest-import\": {\n"
"    \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"path\": \"path/to/package2\",\n"
"      \"alias\": \"pkg2\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:276
msgid "Maximum Concurrent Tests"
msgstr "最大同時テスト数"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:278
msgid ""
"The `max-concurrent-tests` field limits how many tests from this package "
"may run at the same time when `moon test` executes the package."
msgstr ""
"`max-concurrent-tests` フィールドは、`moon test` "
"がこのパッケージを実行するときに、このパッケージのテストを同時に実行できる数を制限します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:281
msgid ""
"This is useful when tests in the same package share ports, temporary "
"files, or other external resources that should not all run in parallel."
msgstr "同じパッケージ内のテストがポート、一時ファイル、または同時実行すべきでないその他の外部リソースを共有する場合に便利です。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:286
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"max-concurrent-tests\": 2,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:293
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"max-concurrent-tests\": 2\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:301
msgid "Conditional Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:303
msgid "The smallest unit of conditional compilation is a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:305
msgid ""
"In a conditional compilation expression, three logical operators are "
"supported: `and`, `or`, and `not`, where the `or` operator can be "
"omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:307
msgid ""
"For example, `[\"or\", \"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"]` can be simplified to "
"`[\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:309
msgid ""
"Conditions in the expression can be categorized into backends and "
"optimization levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:311
msgid "**Backend conditions**: `\"wasm\"`, `\"wasm-gc\"`, and `\"js\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:312
msgid "**Optimization level conditions**: `\"debug\"` and `\"release\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:314
msgid "Conditional expressions support nesting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:316
msgid ""
"If a file is not listed in `\"targets\"`, it will be compiled under all "
"conditions by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:322
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  targets: {\n"
"    \"only_js.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm_gc.mbt\": [\"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"all_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"not_js.mbt\": [\"not\", \"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_debug.mbt\": [\"debug\"],\n"
"    \"js_and_release.mbt\": [\"and\", [\"js\"], [\"release\"]],\n"
"    \"js_only_test.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"js_or_wasm.mbt\": [\"js\", \"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"wasm_release_or_js_debug.mbt\": [\"or\", [\"and\", \"wasm\", "
"\"release\"], [\"and\", \"js\", \"debug\"]]\n"
"  }\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:341
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"targets\": {\n"
"    \"only_js.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm_gc.mbt\": [\"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"all_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"not_js.mbt\": [\"not\", \"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_debug.mbt\": [\"debug\"],\n"
"    \"js_and_release.mbt\": [\"and\", [\"js\"], [\"release\"]],\n"
"    \"js_only_test.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"js_or_wasm.mbt\": [\"js\", \"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"wasm_release_or_js_debug.mbt\": [\"or\", [\"and\", \"wasm\", "
"\"release\"], [\"and\", \"js\", \"debug\"]]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:360
msgid "Supported Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:362
msgid ""
"The `supported_targets` field declares which backends a package is "
"intended to support. It uses a target-set expression, not an array:"
msgstr ""
"`supported_targets` "
"フィールドは、パッケージが対応する予定のバックエンドを宣言します。値には配列ではなく、ターゲット集合式を使います："

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:367
msgid "supported_targets = \"js\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:372
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"supported-targets\": \"js\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:380
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:382
msgid "`js` for a single backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:383
msgid "`+js+wasm-gc` for an explicit set of backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:384
msgid "`+all-js` for all backends except `js`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:386
msgid "Legacy array syntax is still accepted for compatibility:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:390
msgid "supported_targets = [\"js\", \"native\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:395
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"supported-targets\": [\"js\", \"native\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:403
msgid "This is package metadata, not a conditional compilation rule:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:405
msgid "use `supported_targets` to declare the package's supported backend set"
msgstr "`supported_targets` を使って、パッケージが対応するバックエンド集合を宣言する"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:406
msgid ""
"use `targets` to include or exclude individual files for different "
"backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:407
msgid ""
"use `preferred_target` in `moon.mod` to choose the default backend for "
"commands such as `moon check`, `moon run`, and `moon build`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:409
msgid ""
"When both the module and the package declare `supported_targets`, the "
"effective backend set is their intersection."
msgstr "モジュールとパッケージの両方で `supported_targets` を宣言した場合、有効なバックエンド集合は両方の宣言の積集合になります。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:412
msgid "Command behavior follows the selected backend:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:414
msgid ""
"`moon check`, `moon build`, `moon test`, and `moon bench` keep only "
"packages that support the selected backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:415
msgid "`moon run` requires the selected package to support the selected backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:416
msgid "`moon info` skips unsupported selected packages with a warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:417
msgid ""
"`moon bundle` skips package targets that do not support the selected "
"backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:419
msgid ""
"After root selection, Moon also checks reachable required dependencies. "
"If a required dependency does not support the selected backend, the "
"command fails with a normal user-facing error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:422
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:424
msgid "omitting `supported_targets` means all backends are supported"
msgstr "`supported_targets` を省略すると、すべてのバックエンドがサポート対象になる"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:425
msgid ""
"`--target all` expands to `wasm`, `wasm-gc`, `js`, and `native`, but not "
"`llvm`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:426
msgid "`llvm` is still a valid `supported_targets` value"
msgstr "`llvm` も `supported_targets` の有効な値である"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:427
msgid "legacy array syntax is deprecated, but still accepted for compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:429
msgid "A common setup is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:431
msgid "mark a native-only package with `supported_targets = \"native\"`"
msgstr "native 専用パッケージには `supported_targets = \"native\"` を設定する"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:432
msgid "set `preferred_target = \"native\"` in `moon.mod`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:433
msgid "use `targets` only when some files inside the package differ by backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:435
msgid "Native Stub Files"
msgstr "ネイティブスタブファイル"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:437
msgid ""
"The `native-stub` field lists C stub source files that should be compiled"
" with this package for native builds."
msgstr "`native-stub` フィールドは、native ビルド向けにこのパッケージと一緒にコンパイルすべき C スタブソースファイルを列挙します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:440
msgid ""
"This is commonly used together with [`extern \"C\"` declarations in the "
"FFI documentation](../../language/ffi.md), where the stub file provides "
"wrapper functions or adapter code that is easier to write in C than "
"directly in MoonBit."
msgstr ""
"これは、[FFI ドキュメントにある `extern \"C\"` 宣言](../../language/ffi.md) "
"と組み合わせて使われることが多く、その場合スタブファイルは、MoonBit で直接書くより C "
"で書く方が容易なラッパー関数やアダプタコードを提供します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:445
msgid "Paths are relative to the package directory."
msgstr "パスはパッケージディレクトリからの相対パスです。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:449
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"native-stub\": [ \"stub.c\", \"helpers.c\" ],\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:456
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"native-stub\": [\"stub.c\", \"helpers.c\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:464
msgid "Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:466
msgid ""
"Packages declared as `executable` or `foreign_library` produce linked "
"output. The boolean `link: true` form is legacy; use `pkgtype(kind: "
"\"foreign_library\")` when a package builds a library for foreign code. "
"An object-valued `link` option configures backend-specific linking."
msgstr ""
"`executable` または `foreign_library` として宣言されたパッケージは、リンク済みの出力を生成します。ブール値形式の "
"`link: true` は旧形式です。外部コード向けのライブラリをビルドする場合は `pkgtype(kind: "
"\"foreign_library\")` を使用してください。オブジェクト形式の `link` "
"オプションはバックエンド固有のリンク設定に使用します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:471
msgid ""
"The `link` option is used to specify link options, and its value can be "
"either a boolean or an object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:473
msgid ""
"Currently, `link` does not work for the native backend. The behavior "
"described in this section applies to the `wasm`, `wasm-gc`, and `js` "
"backends."
msgstr ""
"現在、`link` は native バックエンドでは動作しません。この節で説明する挙動は `wasm`、`wasm-gc`、`js` "
"バックエンドに適用されます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:476
msgid ""
"For new function exports, prefer [`#export_name`](/language/attributes.md"
"#export-name-attribute). Use the backend-specific `exports` field when "
"the export set or names must differ by backend, or when the source cannot"
" be annotated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:481
msgid ""
"When the `link` value is `true`, it indicates that the package should be "
"linked. The output will vary depending on the backend specified during "
"the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:485
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: true\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:492
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": true\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:500
msgid ""
"When the `link` value is an object, it indicates that the package should "
"be linked, and you can specify link options. For detailed configuration, "
"please refer to the subpage for the corresponding backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:502
msgid "Wasm Backend Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:504
msgid "Common Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:506
msgid ""
"The `exports` option is used to specify the function names exported by "
"the Wasm backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:508
msgid ""
"For example, in the following configuration, the `hello` function from "
"the current package is exported as the `hello` function in the Wasm "
"module, and the `foo` function is exported as the `bar` function in the "
"Wasm module. In the Wasm host, the `hello` and `bar` functions can be "
"called to invoke the `hello` and `foo` functions from the current "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:512
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [ \"hello\", \"foo:bar\" ],\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [ \"hello\", \"foo:bar\" ],\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:526
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [\n"
"        \"hello\",\n"
"        \"foo:bar\"\n"
"      ]\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [\n"
"        \"hello\",\n"
"        \"foo:bar\"\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:547
msgid ""
"The `import-memory` option is used to specify the linear memory imported "
"by the Wasm module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:549
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration specifies that the linear memory"
" imported by the Wasm module is the `memory` variable from the `env` "
"module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:553
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"import-memory\": {\n"
"        \"module\": \"env\",\n"
"        \"name\": \"memory\",\n"
"      },\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"import-memory\": {\n"
"        \"module\": \"env\",\n"
"        \"name\": \"memory\",\n"
"      },\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:573
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"import-memory\": {\n"
"        \"module\": \"env\",\n"
"        \"name\": \"memory\"\n"
"      }\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"import-memory\": {\n"
"        \"module\": \"env\",\n"
"        \"name\": \"memory\"\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:594
msgid ""
"The `memory-limits` option is used to specify the minimum and maximum "
"size of the linear memory used by the Wasm module."
msgstr "`memory-limits` オプションは、Wasm モジュールが使用する線形メモリの最小サイズと最大サイズを指定するために使います。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:597
msgid "The `shared-memory` option is used to enable shared linear memory."
msgstr "`shared-memory` オプションは、共有線形メモリを有効にするために使います。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:599
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration sets memory limits and enables "
"shared memory for both the `wasm` and `wasm-gc` backends."
msgstr "たとえば、次の設定では `wasm` と `wasm-gc` の両バックエンドに対してメモリ制限を設定し、共有メモリを有効にしています。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:604
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"memory-limits\": {\n"
"        \"min\": 1,\n"
"        \"max\": 65536,\n"
"      },\n"
"      \"shared-memory\": true,\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"memory-limits\": {\n"
"        \"min\": 1,\n"
"        \"max\": 65535,\n"
"      },\n"
"      \"shared-memory\": true,\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:626
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"memory-limits\": {\n"
"        \"min\": 1,\n"
"        \"max\": 65536\n"
"      },\n"
"      \"shared-memory\": true\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"memory-limits\": {\n"
"        \"min\": 1,\n"
"        \"max\": 65535\n"
"      },\n"
"      \"shared-memory\": true\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:649
msgid ""
"The `export-memory-name` option is used to specify the name of the linear"
" memory exported by the Wasm module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:653
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"export-memory-name\": \"memory\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"export-memory-name\": \"memory\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:667
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"export-memory-name\": \"memory\"\n"
"    },\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"export-memory-name\": \"memory\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:682
msgid "Wasm Linear Backend Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:684
msgid ""
"The `heap-start-address` option is used to specify the starting address "
"of the linear memory that can be used when compiling to the Wasm backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:686
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration sets the starting address of the"
" linear memory to 1024."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:690
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"heap-start-address\": 1024,\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:701
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm\": {\n"
"      \"heap-start-address\": 1024\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:713
msgid "Wasm GC Backend Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:715
msgid ""
"The `use-js-builtin-string` option is used to specify whether the [JS "
"String Builtin Proposal](https://github.com/WebAssembly/js-string-"
"builtins/blob/main/proposals/js-string-builtins/Overview.md) should be "
"enabled when compiling to the Wasm GC backend. It will make the `String` "
"in MoonBit equivalent to the `String` in JavaScript host runtime."
msgstr ""
"`use-js-builtin-string` オプションは、Wasm GC バックエンドへコンパイルする際に [JS String "
"Builtin Proposal](https://github.com/WebAssembly/js-string-"
"builtins/blob/main/proposals/js-string-builtins/Overview.md) "
"を有効にするかどうかを指定します。これにより、MoonBit の `String` は JavaScript ホストランタイムの `String`"
" と等価になります。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:718
msgid "For example, the following configuration enables the JS String Builtin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:722
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"use-js-builtin-string\": true,\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:733
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"use-js-builtin-string\": true\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:745
msgid ""
"The `imported-string-constants` option is used to specify the imported "
"string namespace used by the JS String Builtin Proposal, which is \"_\" "
"by default. It should meet the configuration in the JS host runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:748
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration and JS initialization configures"
" the imported string namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:752
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"use-js-builtin-string\": true,\n"
"      \"imported-string-constants\": \"_\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:764
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"wasm-gc\": {\n"
"      \"use-js-builtin-string\": true,\n"
"      \"imported-string-constants\": \"_\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:777
msgid ""
"const { instance } = await WebAssembly.instantiate(bytes, {}, { "
"importedStringConstants: \"strings\" });\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:781
msgid "JS Backend Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:783
msgid ""
"The `exports` option is used to specify the function names to export in "
"the JavaScript module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:785
msgid ""
"For example, in the following configuration, the `hello` function from "
"the current package is exported as the `hello` function in the JavaScript"
" module. In the JavaScript host, the `hello` function can be called to "
"invoke the `hello` function from the current package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:789
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"js\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [ \"hello\" ],\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:800
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"js\": {\n"
"      \"exports\": [\n"
"        \"hello\"\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:814
msgid ""
"The `format` option is used to specify the output format of the "
"JavaScript module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:816
msgid "The currently supported formats are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:817
msgid "`esm` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:818
msgid "`cjs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:819
msgid "`iife`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:821
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration sets the output format of the "
"current package to ES Module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:825
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"js\": {\n"
"      \"format\": \"esm\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:836
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"js\": {\n"
"      \"format\": \"esm\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:848
msgid "Native Backend Link Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:850
msgid ""
"The `cc` option is used to specify the compiler for compiling the "
"`moonc`-generated C source files. It can be either a full path to the "
"compiler or a simple name that is accessible via the PATH environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:855
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc\": \"/usr/bin/gcc13\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:866
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc\": \"/usr/bin/gcc13\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:878
msgid ""
"The `cc-flags` option is used to override the default flags passed to the"
" compiler. For example, you can use the following flag to define a macro "
"called MOONBIT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:883
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc-flags\": \"-DMOONBIT\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:894
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc-flags\": \"-DMOONBIT\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:906
msgid ""
"The `cc-link-flags` option is used to override the default flags passed "
"to the linker. Since the linker is invoked through the compiler driver "
"(e.g., `cc` instead of `ld`, `cl` instead of `link`), you should prefix "
"specific options with `-Wl,` or `/link ` when passing them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:910
msgid "The following example strips symbol information from produced binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:914
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  link: {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc-link-flags\": \"-s\",\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:925
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"link\": {\n"
"    \"native\": {\n"
"      \"cc-link-flags\": \"-s\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:937
msgid ""
"The `stub-cc` option is similar to `cc` but controls which compiler to "
"use for compiling stubs. Although it can be different from `cc`, it is "
"not recommended and should only be used for debugging purposes. "
"Therefore, we strongly recommend to specify `cc` and `stub-cc` at the "
"same time and make them consistent to avoid potential conflicts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:942
msgid ""
"The `stub-cc-flags` is similar to `cc-flags`. It only have effects on "
"stubs compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:944
msgid ""
"The `stub-cc-link-flags` are similar but have a subtle difference.  "
"Normally, stubs are compiled into object files and linked against object "
"files generated from `moonc`-generated C source files.  This linking is "
"only controlled by `cc-flags` and `cc-link-flags`, as mentioned earlier."
"  However, in specific modes, such as when the fast-debugging-test "
"feature is enabled, there will be a separate linking procedure for stub "
"objects files, where  `stub-cc-link-flags` will take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:951
msgid "Default C compiler and compiler flags for the native backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:953
msgid ""
"Here is a brief summarization to "
"[compiler_flags.rs](https://github.com/moonbitlang/moon/blob/main/crates/moonutil/src/compiler_flags.rs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:955
msgid "C Compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:957
msgid ""
"On Windows, the native backend requires an MSVC-compatible toolchain with"
" C++ tools and the Windows SDK. Both Microsoft `cl.exe` and LLVM `clang-"
"cl.exe` are supported. MinGW toolchains are not supported."
msgstr ""
"Windows では、native バックエンドに C++ ツールと Windows SDK を含む MSVC 互換ツールチェーンが必要です。"
"Microsoft の `cl.exe` と LLVM の `clang-cl.exe` の両方をサポートしています。MinGW ツールチェーンはサポートされていません。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:961
msgid ""
"On other platforms, Moon searches PATH for the following items from top "
"to bottom."
msgstr "その他のプラットフォームでは、Moon は PATH から次の項目を上から順に検索します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:964
msgid "gcc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:965
msgid "clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:966
msgid "cc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:968
msgid ""
"For GCC-like compilers, the default compile & link command is as follows."
" `[]` is used to indicate the flags may not exist in some modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:970
msgid ""
"cc -o $target -I$MOON_HOME/include -L$MOON_HOME/lib [-g] [-shared -fPIC] "
"\\\n"
"   -fwrapv -fno-strict-aliasing (-O2|-Og) "
"[$MOON_HOME/lib/libmoonbitrun.o] \\\n"
"   $sources -lm $cc_flags $cc_link_flags\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:976
msgid ""
"For MSVC-compatible compiler drivers on Windows, the default compile & "
"link command is as follows."
msgstr "Windows 上の MSVC 互換コンパイラドライバでは、デフォルトのコンパイルおよびリンクコマンドは次のとおりです。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:978
msgid ""
"cl (/Fo|/Fe)$target -I$MOON_HOME/include [/LD] /utf-8 /wd4819 /nologo "
"(/O2|/Od) \\\n"
"   /link /LIBPATH:$MOON_HOME/lib\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:983
msgid "Rule and dev_build"
msgstr "rule と dev_build"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:985
msgid ""
"`rule` declares a reusable command, and `dev_build` applies a rule to "
"concrete input and output files. These pre-build steps run before "
"development commands such as `moon check`, `moon build`, and `moon test`."
msgstr ""
"`rule` は再利用可能なコマンドを宣言し、`dev_build` は具体的な入力ファイルと出力ファイルに `rule` "
"を適用します。これらの事前ビルドステップは、`moon check`、`moon build`、`moon test` "
"などの開発用コマンドの前に実行されます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:989
msgid ""
"This mechanism is intended for package authors during package "
"development. When the package is used as a dependency by downstream "
"users, these pre-build steps are not triggered for security reasons, so "
"dependencies do not execute arbitrary commands during builds. Commit the "
"generated output files to the repository so downstream users can build "
"against them directly."
msgstr "この仕組みは、パッケージ作者がパッケージ開発中に使用することを想定しています。そのパッケージが下流ユーザーの依存関係として使われる場合、セキュリティ上の理由から、これらの事前ビルドステップは実行されません。そのため、依存関係がビルド中に任意のコマンドを実行することはありません。生成された出力ファイルをリポジトリにコミットし、下流ユーザーがそれらを直接使ってビルドできるようにしてください。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:995
msgid ""
"`rule(name: \"...\", command: \"...\")` declares a reusable command "
"template. The `name` field identifies the rule, and `command` is a shell "
"command string. The command can refer to `$input` and `$output`, which "
"are supplied by the `dev_build` entry that uses the rule. A package can "
"declare multiple `rule` entries."
msgstr ""
"`rule(name: \"...\", command: \"...\")` は再利用可能なコマンドテンプレートを宣言します。`name` "
"フィールドはその `rule` を識別し、`command` はシェルコマンド文字列です。コマンドは `$input` と `$output` "
"を参照できます。これらは、その `rule` を使用する `dev_build` エントリから提供されます。パッケージは複数の `rule` "
"エントリを宣言できます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1001
msgid ""
"`dev_build(rule: \"...\", input: \"...\", output: \"...\")` declares a "
"pre-build step. It selects a rule and supplies the input and output paths"
" used when expanding that rule's command. A package can declare multiple "
"`dev_build` entries."
msgstr ""
"`dev_build(rule: \"...\", input: \"...\", output: \"...\")` "
"は事前ビルドステップを宣言します。これは `rule` を選択し、その `rule` "
"のコマンドを展開するときに使用する入力パスと出力パスを提供します。パッケージは複数の `dev_build` エントリを宣言できます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1006
msgid ""
"Pre-build commands run with the module root as their working directory. "
"Input, output, and other pre-build paths are resolved relative to that "
"module root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1009
msgid ""
"Rules can be declared either as package-level rules in the same "
"`moon.pkg` or as module-level rules in "
"[`moon.mod`](/toolchain/moon/module.md). A package-level rule is visible "
"only to `dev_build` entries in that same `moon.pkg`; a module-level rule "
"is visible to `dev_build` entries in every package in the module. When "
"resolving a rule name, `moon` first looks for a package-level rule in the"
" same `moon.pkg`, then for a module-level rule in `moon.mod`."
msgstr ""
"`rule` は、同じ `moon.pkg` 内のパッケージレベル `rule` "
"として宣言することも、[`moon.mod`](/toolchain/moon/module.md) 内のモジュールレベル `rule` "
"として宣言することもできます。パッケージレベル `rule` は、同じ `moon.pkg` 内の `dev_build` "
"エントリからのみ参照できます。モジュールレベル `rule` は、モジュール内のすべてのパッケージの `dev_build` "
"エントリから参照できます。`rule` 名を解決するとき、`moon` はまず同じ `moon.pkg` 内のパッケージレベル `rule` "
"を探し、次に `moon.mod` 内のモジュールレベル `rule` を探します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1018
msgid ""
"rule(name: \"copy\", command: \"cat $input > $output\")\n"
"dev_build(rule: \"copy\", input: \"a.txt\", output: \"a.mbt\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1024
msgid ""
"The `rule` and `dev_build` entries are not supported in `moon.pkg.json`. "
"Use the deprecated `pre-build` configuration instead:"
msgstr ""
"`moon.pkg.json` では `rule` エントリと `dev_build` エントリはサポートされていません。代わりに、非推奨の "
"`pre-build` 設定を使用してください："

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1026
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"pre-build\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"input\": \"a.txt\",\n"
"      \"output\": \"a.mbt\",\n"
"      \"command\": \"cat $input > $output\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1040
msgid ""
"In this example, running a development command such as `moon check` "
"copies the contents of `a.txt` to `a.mbt` before the package is checked."
msgstr ""
"この例では、`moon check` などの開発用コマンドを実行すると、パッケージがチェックされる前に `a.txt` の内容が `a.mbt` "
"にコピーされます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1043
msgid "Warnings List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1045
msgid ""
"Warning lists disable or enable warnings. To make enabled warnings fail a"
" command, use `--deny-warn`. A warning list is a string composed of one "
"or more warning names, each prefixed with a sign:"
msgstr ""
"警告リストは警告を無効化または有効化します。有効な警告でコマンドを失敗させるには、`--deny-warn` を使います。警告リストは 1 "
"つ以上の警告名で構成される文字列で、各警告名の先頭に記号を付けます："

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1049
msgid "`-` to disable the warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1050
msgid "`+` to enable the warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1052
msgid ""
"For example, in the following configuration, `-unused_value` disables the"
" unused functions and variables warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1056
msgid "warnings = \"-unused_value\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1061
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"warn-list\": \"-unused_value\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1069
msgid ""
"If multiple warnings need to be disabled, they can be directly connected "
"and combined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1073
msgid "warnings = \"-unused_value-unreachable_code\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1078
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"warn-list\": \"-unused_value-unreachable_code\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1086
msgid ""
"If it is necessary to activate certain warnings that were originally "
"prohibited, use the plus sign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1090
msgid "warnings = \"+unused_optional_argument\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1095
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"warn-list\": \"+unused_optional_argument\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1103
msgid ""
"Older configurations may use an `@` prefix to promote a warning to an "
"error. The prefix remains accepted only for compatibility and should not "
"be used in new configuration. Use `moon check --deny-warn` (and the "
"equivalent flag on other CI commands) when warnings should fail the "
"build."
msgstr ""
"古い設定では、警告をエラーに昇格させるために `@` "
"接頭辞を使っていることがあります。この接頭辞は互換性のためにのみ引き続き受け入れられますが、新しい設定では使用しないでください。警告でビルドを失敗させる場合は、`moon"
" check --deny-warn` （および他の CI コマンドの同等のフラグ）を使います。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1108
msgid ""
"You can also use warning numbers in `warnings`. In the output below, "
"`mnemonic` is the symbolic warning name used in warning lists, while `id`"
" is the numeric form of the same warning."
msgstr "`warnings` では警告番号も使用できます。以下の出力で、`mnemonic` は警告リストで使う記号名、`id` は同じ警告の数値形式です。"

